    "body": "`FlushStateToDisk()` handles block storage directly. It applies `BlockManager`'s prune locks, writes its pruned flag, checks its blocks directory space and runs the flush, index write and file deletion, while `BlockManager` reads the chainstate to pick files. A pruning API on block storage (#35627) would have to go through validation for all of it.\n\nThis moves the storage side into `BlockManager`, as described in the same issue. Validation decides which heights may be pruned and passes them as limits. `BlockManager` applies its prune locks, selects the files, flushes, writes the index and deletes the files, in the same order as before. There is no behavior change to my knowledge.\n\nBased on #36735\n\nThanks to musaHaruna for his [review on my fork](https://github.com/pzafonte/bitcoin/pull/2#pullrequestreview-5533305792), which led to grouping and checking the prune limits and to moving the prune bookkeeping into `BlockManager`.",
